6-part2.webp", "alt": "A woman with open arms in a field at sunset"}], "bullets": ["Describe a day when you felt really happy.", "Where were you and who were you with?", "Why do you still remember that particular day?"]}, {"part": 4, "title": "Everyone should learn to play a musical instrument.", "for": ["improves memory, patience and concentration", "a healthy way to relax and express emotions", "helps people connect through culture and performance"], "against": ["lessons and good instruments are expensive", "takes time away from study or work", "not everyone has the interest or the talent for music"]}, {"part": 1, "title": "Weather and umbrellas", "questions": ["What is your favourite kind of weather?", "Do you often carry an umbrella with you?", "What do you usually do when the weather is bad?"]}, {"part": 2, "title": "Working alone and working in a team", "images": [{"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t07-part12-a.webp", "alt": "A young man working alone at a desk with a computer"}, {"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t07-part12-b.webp", "alt": "A group of colleagues working together around a table"}], "questions": ["What do you see in these pictures?", "What are the differences between working alone and working in a team?", "What are the benefits of working from home compared with working in an office?"]}, {"part": 3, "title": "Waiting a long time", "images": [{"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t07-part2.webp", "alt": "A man in a suit talking on the phone in front of a departures board"}], "bullets": ["Describe a situation when you had to wait a long time for someone or something.", "How did you feel while you were waiting?", "How do you usually react when your plans are delayed?"]}, {"part": 4, "title": "Surveillance cameras should be installed in all public places.", "for": ["helps the police to prevent and to solve crime", "makes people feel safer on streets and public transport", "provides useful evidence in accidents and disputes"], "against": ["a serious loss of personal privacy for ordinary citizens", "recordings can be misused, leaked or sold", "very expensive to install and maintain everywhere"]}, {"part": 1, "title": "Hometown, weekends, seasons", "questions": ["Tell me about an interesting place in your hometown.", "What do you often do at the weekend?", "What is your favourite season?"]}, {"part": 2, "title": "Growing food and buying food", "images": [{"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t08-part12-a.webp", "alt": "A man picking vegetables in a garden"}, {"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t08-part12-b.webp", "alt": "A woman choosing fruit in a supermarket"}], "questions": ["What do you see in these pictures?", "Which do you prefer — growing vegetables yourself or buying them from a shop?", "Why do most people prefer to buy food from markets instead of growing it themselves?"]}, {"part": 3, "title": "A skill learned at home", "images": [{"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t08-part2.webp", "alt": "A parent and a child cooking together in a kitchen"}], "bullets": ["Describe a skill that you learned from a member of your family.", "How long did it take you to learn it?", "How useful is that skill for you today?"]}, {"part": 4, "title": "People should grow more of their own food at home.", "for": ["home-grown food is fresher and free from chemicals", "reduces the monthly food costs of a family", "teaches children where their food actually comes from"], "against": ["most city flats have no land and not enough sunlight", "growing food takes daily time, effort and knowledge", "shops offer far more variety throughout the whole year"]}, {"part": 1, "title": "School, sports, weekends", "questions": ["Tell me about your school.", "Do you like doing any sports?", "What do you do at the weekends?"]}, {"part": 2, "title": "Outdoor and indoor activities", "images": [{"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t09-part12-a.webp", "alt": "Young people playing volleyball on a beach"}, {"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t09-part12-b.webp", "alt": "A family playing a board game at home"}], "questions": ["What do you see in these pictures?", "What are the advantages of outdoor activities?", "Why do some people prefer indoor activities?"]}, {"part": 3, "title": "A time you did not succeed", "images": [{"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t09-part2.webp", "alt": "A tired man rubbing his eyes at a desk in front of a blackboard"}], "bullets": ["Tell me about a situation when you worked very hard but did not succeed.", "What would you do differently if you had the same chance again?", "How do you usually motivate yourself after a failure?"]}, {"part": 4, "title": "Children should take part in extracurricular activities outside their school lessons.", "for": ["keeps children active, healthy and away from screens", "helps them make friends outside their own classroom", "develops talents that the school programme ignores"], "against": ["children already have a very heavy homework load", "extra activities cost money and require transport", "leaves less time for family, rest and sleep"]}, {"part": 1, "title": "Pets, typical day, first teacher", "questions": ["Do you have any pets?", "What is your typical day like?", "Describe your first teacher."]}, {"part": 2, "title": "Eating in a restaurant and at home", "images": [{"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t10-part12-a.webp", "alt": "Friends laughing and eating burgers outdoors"}, {"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t10-part12-b.webp", "alt": "A woman eating a salad in her kitchen at home"}], "questions": ["What do you see in these pictures?", "Why do many people prefer eating at home?", "What are the advantages of eating in a restaurant?"]}, {"part": 3, "title": "A happy moment", "images": [{"url": "/content/cefr/2026-09/t10-part2.webp", "alt": "A happy family together at an amusement park"}], "bullets": ["Describe a time when you felt happy about something.", "Who was with you at that moment?", "How do happy moments and good relationships help people to achieve things in the future?"]}, {"part": 4, "title": "Everyone should own and learn to play a musical instrument.", "for": ["music develops discipline, creativity and self-expression", "a useful skill for family celebrations and social life", "supports national culture and musical traditions"], "against": ["good quality instruments are costly for most families", "requires years of regular and patient practice", "people can enjoy music fully without playing it"]}], "mock_sets": [{"name": "CEFR-1", "sort_order": 1, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "First teacher, typical day, pets"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Eating out and eating at home"}, {"part": 3, "title": "A truly happy moment"}, {"part": 4, "title": "Students should be encouraged to take part in extracurricular activities."}]}, {"name": "CEFR-2", "sort_order": 2, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "Breakfast, sports, your room"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Exercising outdoors and in a gym"}, {"part": 3, "title": "A happy achievement"}, {"part": 4, "title": "The number of people working remotely should continue to increase."}]}, {"name": "CEFR-3", "sort_order": 3, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "Your home, favourite drink, bedtime"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Travelling by plane and by train"}, {"part": 3, "title": "Trying hard but failing"}, {"part": 4, "title": "Extracurricular activities should be a compulsory part of the school programme."}]}, {"name": "CEFR-4", "sort_order": 4, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "Favourite food, weekends, hometown"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Online and classroom learning"}, {"part": 3, "title": "A failure and its effect"}, {"part": 4, "title": "The rising cost of fuel has a positive effect on the environment."}]}, {"name": "CEFR-5", "sort_order": 5, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "Your house, hobbies, music"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Working in an office and at home"}, {"part": 3, "title": "A time of change"}, {"part": 4, "title": "Governments should ban all forms of gambling."}]}, {"name": "CEFR-6", "sort_order": 6, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "Studies or work, internet, favourite drink"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Traditional and online education"}, {"part": 3, "title": "A happy day"}, {"part": 4, "title": "Everyone should learn to play a musical instrument."}]}, {"name": "CEFR-7", "sort_order": 7, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "Weather and umbrellas"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Working alone and working in a team"}, {"part": 3, "title": "Waiting a long time"}, {"part": 4, "title": "Surveillance cameras should be installed in all public places."}]}, {"name": "CEFR-8", "sort_order": 8, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "Hometown, weekends, seasons"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Growing food and buying food"}, {"part": 3, "title": "A skill learned at home"}, {"part": 4, "title": "People should grow more of their own food at home."}]}, {"name": "CEFR-9", "sort_order": 9, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "School, sports, weekends"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Outdoor and indoor activities"}, {"part": 3, "title": "A time you did not succeed"}, {"part": 4, "title": "Children should take part in extracurricular activities outside their school lessons."}]}, {"name": "CEFR-10", "sort_order": 10, "topics": [{"part": 1, "title": "Pets, typical day, first teacher"}, {"part": 2, "title": "Eating in a restaurant and at home"}, {"part": 3, "title": "A happy moment"}, {"part": 4, "title": "Everyone should own and learn to play a musical instrument."}]}]}$json$::jsonb;
  t jsonb;
  m record;
  mt record;
  q record;
  tid uuid;
  ms uuid;
begin
  -- Topics and their questions
  for t in select * from jsonb_array_elements(d->'topics') loop
    insert into public.topics (exam, part, title, cue_bullets, images, points_for, points_against)
    values (
      'cefr', (t->>'part')::smallint, t->>'title',
      coalesce(array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(t->'bullets')), '{}'),
      coalesce(t->'images', '[]'::jsonb),
      coalesce(array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(t->'for')), '{}'),
      coalesce(array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(t->'against')), '{}')
    )
    on conflict (exam, part, lower(btrim(title))) do update set
      cue_bullets = excluded.cue_bullets,
      images = excluded.images,
      points_for = excluded.points_for,
      points_against = excluded.points_against
    returning id into tid;

    for q in select value as text, ordinality as n
             from jsonb_array_elements_text(coalesce(t->'questions', '[]'::jsonb)) with ordinality loop
      insert into public.questions (topic_id, text, sort_order) values (tid, q.text, q.n)
      on conflict (topic_id, lower(btrim(text))) do nothing;
    end loop;
  end loop;

  -- Mock sets: exactly the four topics of each test, in exam order
  for m in select value as s from jsonb_array_elements(d->'mock_sets') loop
    insert into public.mock_sets (exam, name, sort_order)
    values ('cefr', m.s->>'name', (m.s->>'sort_order')::int)
    on conflict (exam, lower(btrim(name))) do update set sort_order = excluded.sort_order
    returning id into ms;

    delete from public.mock_set_topics where mock_set_id = ms;
    for mt in select value as x, ordinality as n from jsonb_array_elements(m.s->'topics') with ordinality loop
      select id into tid from public.topics
      where exam = 'cefr' and part = (mt.x->>'part')::smallint and lower(btrim(title)) = lower(btrim(mt.x->>'title'));
      insert into public.mock_set_topics (mock_set_id, topic_id, part, sort_order)
      values (ms, tid, (mt.x->>'part')::smallint, mt.n);
    end loop;
  end loop;
end
$seed$;
